.TH tapectl-volume-compact 1  "tapectl-volume-compact " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-volume\-compact \- Interactive compaction: read + write + finish in one flow
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl volume compact\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR] [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-missing\-escrow\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fILABEL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Interactive compaction: read + write + finish in one flow
.PP
Step 3 applies `compact\-finish`\*(Aqs ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 gate and may refuse non\-interactively without `\-\-force`. When it does, the destination tape is already written and sealed and nothing is lost: `volume compact\-finish <SOURCE> \-\-force` completes the flow without re\-reading or re\-writing anything.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Destination volume label. Without it the flow PROMPTS for one, which needs a terminal — pass this to run compaction non\-interactively (issue #146, ADR\-0008\*(Aqs non\-hanging rule)
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Tape device (by\-id path). Defaults to the only configured drive; required when more than one is configured
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-missing\-escrow\fR
See `volume write \-\-allow\-missing\-escrow`
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
See `volume compact\-finish \-\-force` — step 3\*(Aqs ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 gate. With `\-\-to` and this (or the global `\-\-yes`), the whole three\-step flow runs non\-interactively
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept (issue #147)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fILABEL\fR>
Source volume label
